docs/4.examples/handle-session.md:166:With `idleTimeout` set, H3 moves the idle window forward by resealing the session cookie with the reseal time stamped into it. `createdAt` is left untouched, which is what lets `maxAge` still act as a hard cap on top. The cookie `Expires` is set to whichever limit runs out first.
docs/4.examples/handle-session.md:168:If you are coming from `express-session` or `koa-session`, `idleTimeout` is their `rolling` option. The difference is that it carries its own duration instead of reinterpreting `maxAge`, so enabling it does not cost you the absolute limit.
